# Folder boundaries

| Folder | Holds | Never holds |
|---|---|---|
| `Design/` | tokens, shared controls, `BeruIcon` | feature logic |
| `Engine/` | providers, prompts, registries, diff | SwiftUI `View`s |
| `Panel/` | the floating panel only | app-wide tokens |
| `Dashboard/` | settings window and its pages | secret handling |
| `Settings/` | `SettingsStore`, `KeychainStore` | dashboard pages |
| `Capture` `Speech` `Vault` `Logging` `Support` | one concern each | cross-imports upward |

A type belongs where its only consumer lives. A SwiftUI `View` never lives in
`Engine/`.

# Observation

One convention for shared `@Observable` singletons:

```swift
// GOOD
@Bindable private var settings = SettingsStore.shared

// BAD - a plain property can miss updates
private var registry = TargetRegistry.shared

// BAD - fake observation that only refreshes by accident
let _ = SettingsStore.shared.primaryColorID
```

Do not add a new `static let shared`. Prefer injecting the dependency; the
`shared_singletons` guard counts them.

# Single source of truth

A default value is declared once and referenced everywhere else. The default
local model id lives on `RecommendedOllamaModel`; `SettingsStore` and
`OllamaPullService` read it rather than repeating the string.

# File size

Split anything over 400 lines by responsibility, not by line count. The
`oversized_files` guard tracks this.

# Secrets and network

`KeychainStore` is the only place secrets are persisted, and only
`SettingsStore` may reach it. Network calls go to the configured provider only.
No analytics, no telemetry. Changes here need a look at `SECURITY.md`.
